   "note": "described from Claude's knowledge of the board, not a datasheet"
  },
  "note": "It has no USB port, so you upload through a 5 V USB-serial (FTDI-style) adapter on the 6-pin header with DTR for auto-reset, choosing 'Arduino Pro or Pro Mini, ATmega328P 5V 16MHz' in the IDE. It has the same pin numbers as the Uno but not its header layout, A6/A7 are analog-input only, and A4/A5 (I2C) and A6/A7 sit off the main side rows on many versions."
 },
